Package: os7-powershell
Version: @OS7_VERSION@
Architecture: @OS7_ARCH@
Maintainer: Bastian Wirth <bastian.wirth@upinblue.com>
Section: shells
Priority: important
Depends: @OS7_ICU@, ca-certificates, less, locales
Provides: powershell
Homepage: https://github.com/upinblue/os7
Description: PowerShell 7 as OS/7's interactive shell
 Microsoft's PowerShell 7 release for Linux, repacked from the upstream tarball
 pinned by version and SHA256 in the OS/7 release pin, plus the profile drop-in
 that hands an interactive human session over to it.
 .
 REPACKED RATHER THAN TAKEN FROM MICROSOFT'S APT REPOSITORY, because that
 repository has no snapshot service: a machine that resolved PowerShell from it
 would move independently of the OS/7 release train, and the version number
 would stop describing the system. A Microsoft component moving upstream is a
 release event here, not a background occurrence.
 .
 Bash remains the system shell. The hand-off is a /etc/profile.d drop-in with
 five guards on it — interactive shells only, never an ssh command, never
 re-entrant, never when pwsh is missing, and an OS7_NO_PWSH opt-out — so that
 scp, sftp, cron, dpkg hooks and Intune's own bash compliance scripts all keep
 the shell they expect.
